# bat -- `cat` with syntax highlighting. Used directly, and as the previewer
# behind fzf and delta, so its theme is more visible than it looks.

# Rosé Pine. bat ships no rose-pine theme; themes/rose-pine.tmTheme is the
# tmtheme from the yazi flavor (same upstream, rose-pine/yazi), which is a
# plain TextMate theme and works unmodified here.
#
# A custom theme only takes effect after `bat cache --build`, which compiles
# themes/ into ~/.cache/bat/themes.bin. Re-run it after changing the file --
# editing the .tmTheme alone does nothing.
--theme="rose-pine"

# Show line numbers and git modification markers, but no heavy box drawing.
--style="numbers,changes,header"

# Don't wrap; long lines scroll. Easier to read code and diffs.
--wrap=never
